{"id":"devopshero-7yj","title":"Fix ask_user tool: handle choices as JSON string","description":"## Bug\n\nThe `mcp__devopshero__ask_user` MCP tool fails with `'str' object has no attribute 'get'` error.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nIn `devopshero_app/services/agent/tools/ask_user.py` (lines 63-69), the code assumes `choices` is `list[dict]` but the model passes:\n1. A JSON string that needs parsing (e.g., `\"[\\\"option1\\\", \\\"option2\\\"]\"`)\n2. Simple strings instead of dicts (e.g., `[\"option1\", \"option2\"]` instead of `[{\"id\": \"...\", \"label\": \"option1\"}]`)\n\nThe failing code:\n```python\nfor i, choice in enumerate(choices):\n    processed_choice = {\n        \"id\": choice.get(\"id\", str(uuid.uuid4())),  # Fails: string has no .get()\n        \"label\": choice[\"label\"],                   # Fails: string subscript fails\n        ...\n    }\n```\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd input normalization at the start of `ask_user()`:\n1. Parse `choices` if it's a JSON string\n2. Convert simple string choices to dict format (use string as label, generate UUID for id)\n\n## Files\n- `devopshero_app/services/agent/tools/ask_user.py` - Add input normalization before processing loop\n\n## Verification\n- Test with JSON string choices\n- Test with simple string list\n- Test with proper dict list\n- Verify CHOICE message renders interactive buttons in UI","status":"open","priority":2,"issue_type":"bug","created_at":"2026-01-11T19:37:48.75539-08:00","created_by":"vmendi","updated_at":"2026-01-11T19:37:58.266925-08:00"}
